- op: discuss  # 9432
  at: '2026-09-20T11:02:51Z'  # 9432
  by: agent  # 9432
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9432
  clock: 7  # 9432
  nonce: '9432'  # 9432
  message: "PARTIALLY DONE, DELIBERATELY. Two of the ~58 files are fixed because they had a consumer; the rest is untouched and this row stays open. Re-scoping rather than closing, and saying which part.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT FIRST, because this row's framing understates the problem. This row says `derived_from` is unpopulated at ~20 linker construction sites. On this repository today, before the change:\n\n  edges with `derived_from` populated : 48,879\n  of those, exactly `[edge.src, edge.dst]`: 48,873 — **100.0%**\n  of those, containing ANY edge reference:      **0**\n\nSo the field is not mostly-missing; where it is populated it is TAUTOLOGICAL, which is WI-ratun's finding (filed `wont_do` as a dedup against this row) reproduced independently. `grep -h \"derived_from=\" linkers/*.py | sort | uniq -c` shows the shape directly: `[src_sym.id, c_sym.id]`, `[pub_id, sub_id]`, `[edge.src, resolved_target.id]` — in every case the emitted edge's own two endpoints under different names. A consumer reading it learns nothing the edge did not already say, and a transitive traversal terminates at depth 1 because the targets are Symbols with no `derived_from` of their own.\n\nWHAT LANDED, and why only this much. ADR-0057 §14.1 (WI-togad) gave the field its first consumer: a resolved edge that NAMES the unresolved edge it consumed demotes that stub, with no name-or-line matching. That needs the two recovery passes to record what they actually consumed, so:\n\n  inherited_calls.py       5 sites  [edge.src, <target>.id]   -> [edge.id, <the class the walk started from>]\n  method_call_recovery.py  1 site   [caller_id, chosen_method.id] -> [ucall.id, chosen_hint.id]\n\nAfter: 393 edges carry an edge reference, where the corpus had zero. Tautological share 100.0% -> 99.2%.\n\nWHAT IS NOT DONE. The other ~56 files. Each needs a judgement about what its real upstream evidence IS — the matched config-file path, the decorator AST node, the registry lookup, the consumed edge — and that is not mechanical: `[src_sym.id, c_sym.id]` is wrong in the same way at every site but right-by-accident at none, so each site has to be read. I did not do it in this PR for three reasons, in order of weight:\n\n  1. NO CONSUMER. §14.1 is the field's only reader. Populating the other 56 correctly would produce data nothing reads, and the project's own rule is that a vocabulary value with no producer and a consumer with no producer are the same defect. The inverse — a producer with no consumer — is cheaper but still unverifiable: nothing would go red if I got a site wrong.\n  2. NOT VERIFIABLE PER SITE. With a consumer, a wrong `derived_from` shows up as a wrong demotion. Without one, correctness is a code-reading claim.\n  3. It would put ~56 files of judgement-heavy diff in a PR whose point is a supersession rule.\n\nWHAT I RECOMMEND. Drive the remaining sweep from consumers, not from the field: when a second reader of `derived_from` lands, populate the linkers that reader needs, and let its assertions be what proves each site right. If the owner wants the sweep done regardless, say so and I will do it as its own PR — but it should be split by linker family, not landed as one 56-file change.\n\nALSO: WI-ratun is `wont_do` as a dedup against this row, and its tranch_04 entry flags for the operator that the mechanism is live. This entry is the measurement it asked for; the mechanism is still live for ~56 files."  # 9432
