- op: discuss  # 2c2f
  at: '2026-09-21T08:50:14Z'  # 2c2f
  by: agent  # 2c2f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2c2f
  clock: 9  # 2c2f
  nonce: 2c2f  # 2c2f
  message: "STALE `isbefore` REMOVED: WI-togad-gusab-togul-vumaj-habov-vurat-bifut-gohur.\n\nThis row declared that it BLOCKS WI-togad. WI-togad closed `done` on 2026-09-20 -- it shipped ADR-0057 section 14.1 without waiting, because the only two construction sites its finalize step needed (`inherited_calls.py`, 5 sites; `method_call_recovery.py`, 1 site) are exactly the two this row populated the same day. The dependency outlived the thing it was protecting.\n\nWhy it mattered rather than being cosmetic: a blocker pointing at a CLOSED row is a link `ready` can never satisfy and can never clear. It reads to a future agent as \"there is downstream work waiting on the other ~56 files\", which is the opposite of the truth recorded in my 2026-09-20 entry -- the remaining sweep has NO consumer waiting on it, and that is the stated reason it was not done.\n\nNOTHING ELSE CHANGES. Still `todo_hard`, still 2 of ~58 files, still recommended to be driven FROM a second consumer of `derived_from` rather than from the field, so that a wrong site shows up as a wrong demotion instead of as an unverifiable code-reading claim. That recommendation -- and the offer to do the ~56-file sweep as its own family-split PR if the owner wants it regardless -- is still unanswered."  # 2c2f
- op: discuss  # f098
  at: '2026-09-22T01:28:55Z'  # f098
  by: agent  # f098
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f098
  clock: 10  # f098
  nonce: f098  # f098
  message: "PREMISES RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21. The row is NOT stale -- the work is genuinely\nundone -- but EVERY NUMBER IN IT IS WRONG, and it is filed as the wrong KIND of\nproblem. Re-file before working it.\n\n1. THE COVERAGE FIGURE COUNTS VACUOUS VALUES AS POPULATED.\nMeasured on .hypergumbo/self-analysis.json:\n\n    edges                                        190,109\n    derived_from populated                        45,204  (23.8%)\n      of those, == the edge's own [src, dst]      44,813  (99.1%)\n    carrying anything beyond the endpoints           391  ( 0.2%)\n\n    real provenance comes from exactly two passes:\n      inherited-calls-linker        329\n      method-call-recovery-linker    62\n    the vacuous bulk is one pass:\n      containment-linker         44,104  (`contains` edges)\n\nSo coverage is 0.2%, not ~22%. The row's \"23,737 of 109,849 (~22%)\" is counting\nedges whose derived_from restates their own endpoints and therefore carries no\nderivation information whatsoever.\n\n2. THE SCOPE FIGURE IS WRONG, AND THE JOB IS NOT MECHANICAL.\nAST scan of packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/:\n\n    Edge.create sites passing derived_from      93  across 58 linker files\n      passing literally [src, dst]              86\n      passing anything richer                    7   (inheritance.py:350,\n        inherited_calls.py x5, method_call_recovery.py:401)\n\nNot \"~20 linker files\", and not \"add derived_from= at each site\" -- the kwarg is\nALREADY THERE at 93 of 93 sites. The work is replacing a vacuous value with a\nreal one, which is a per-linker semantic question, not a mechanical sweep. The\nrow's own prescribed fix (\"the fix is mechanical (add derived_from=[source_id_a,\nsource_id_b, ...])\") is the exact pattern that produced the 44,104 vacuous rows,\nand following it literally would entrench them.\n\n3. IT IS A FALSE-CLAIM BUG, NOT A COVERAGE GAP, AND IT HAS A USER-FACING SURFACE.\n`hypergumbo explain --provenance` (cli.py::_print_edge_provenance) prints\nderived_from as a derivation chain. For the 44,813 vacuous edges it prints the\nedge's own two endpoints dressed as provenance; for edges with none it prints the\nhonest \"(no derivation chain -- analyzer-produced edge)\". The display is\ninverted: the uninformative ones look documented.\nThe other consumer is SAFE, but only by luck of type: finalize.py's ADR-0057\nSec 14.1 stub demotion acts only on a ref naming an unresolved EDGE, and\n[src, dst] are SYMBOL ids, so the vacuous values miss the lookup and cause no\nfalse demotions. Worth knowing before anyone \"fixes\" derived_from to hold edge\nids.\n\n4. PARENTAGE IS WRONG. This row's parent is INV-nuzal, which is satisfied and is\nabout node.quality / edge.provenance -- a different field. The real parent is\nINV-rukor (the row that added derived_from). See the note I am filing there:\nINV-rukor was closed `satisfied` on 2026-07-26 on a guard test that only asserts\nthe derived_from= KWARG IS PRESENT at each Edge.create site\n(test_edge_derived_from.py::_find_edge_create_calls_missing_derived_from checks\n`if \"derived_from\" not in kwarg_names`), which cannot distinguish [src, dst] from\na real consumed-id list. That closure also states \"WI-latup not in repo\" -- this\nrow exists and is open. Its own earlier validation (2026-06-05) had already\nmeasured the degeneracy and set it violated at blind severity 4.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: that any consumer is currently producing a wrong ANALYSIS because of\nthis. The measured harm is a misleading --provenance display and a field that\nreads as populated while carrying nothing."  # f098
- op: discuss  # f0f7
  at: '2026-09-22T06:27:27Z'  # f0f7
  by: agent  # f0f7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f0f7
  clock: 11  # f0f7
  nonce: f0f7  # f0f7
  message: "PARTIAL: the DISCLOSURE half shipped, the POPULATION half did not. This row stays open, because its stated deliverable is population.\n\nSHIPPED (merged to dev): 'explain --provenance' no longer presents an endpoints-only derived_from as a derivation chain. Three states now get three messages -- a real chain, an endpoints-only restatement, and nothing at all. Endpoints-only is kept DISTINCT from carrying-nothing rather than folded into it, because a linker did run and did record a value; collapsing them would hide that. The check is a SUBSET test, not equality, because inheritance.py:350 passes a one-element list holding the edge's own source.\n\nOnly the reader's view changed. No producer output changed and nothing was discarded. finalize.py's ADR-0057 Sec 14.1 consumer was already immune by type -- it acts only on a ref naming an unresolved EDGE, and [src, dst] are SYMBOL ids -- so the vacuous values never caused a false demotion.\n\nSTILL OPEN, and re-scoped by measurement rather than by the row's original text:\n  93 Edge.create sites across 58 linker files ALREADY pass derived_from\n  86 of them pass literally [src, dst]\n   7 pass something richer (inheritance.py:350, inherited_calls.py x5, method_call_recovery.py:401)\nSo the job is NOT 'add the kwarg at ~20 sites' -- the kwarg is present at 93 of 93. It is replacing a vacuous value with a real one, which is a per-linker semantic question about what each pass actually consumed. The row's prescribed fix (derived_from=[source_id_a, source_id_b, ...]) is the exact pattern that produced the 44,104 vacuous rows, and following it literally would entrench them.\n\nA WARNING FOR WHOEVER TAKES THE POPULATION HALF: for containment-linker, [src, dst] may be the HONEST answer -- a containment edge really is derived from just the parent and the child. There the right outcome is probably to record nothing rather than to invent a third input. But INV-rukor's guard test asserts every linker Edge.create passes derived_from=, so 'record nothing' would FAIL that test. The test that closed INV-rukor is what keeps the field vacuous. That interaction has to be resolved before the population work can proceed, and it is part of why I did not sweep.\n\nSee the note on INV-rukor: it was closed satisfied on that same syntactic guard, which cannot witness the semantic half of its own statement. Owner's ruling still requested there."  # f0f7
- op: discuss  # 8832
  at: '2026-09-22T21:36:31Z'  # 8832
  by: agent  # 8832
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8832
  clock: 12  # 8832
  nonce: '8832'  # 8832
  message: "POPULATION HALF, FAMILY 1: MERGED as PR #1134 (562e5a3b8b). The row stays open for family 2 (the 9 `incomplete` sites).\n\nThe coupling this row raised is resolved: \"where [src,dst] is honest, record nothing -- but INV-rukor's guard forbids it\". Honest endpoints-only is now a DECLARED value (`# derived-from endpoints: <reason>`), not None. A linker that consumed nothing records `[]` (schema 0.20.13). The guard reads values and requires the declaration. See INV-rukor for the rule and the evidence.\n\nAll 86 endpoints-only sites were classified by reading them. It was not a sweep:\n  17 now name the consumed record, 24 declared honest, 36 dropped minted ids, 9 declared incomplete.\nMeasured on a self-survey: real chains 399 -> 840. type-hierarchy 342/342 is now a chain. Per-linker edge counts are unchanged.\n\nNEXT (family 2): make `_transitive_bases` keep the ancestor and edge ids it walks, and thread them into the 6 callers. Then _view_template_core's controller class, the DI heuristic binding edge, and the fire.Fire class.\n\nThe row's parent is INV-nuzal, which the 09-22 audit showed is the wrong parent (INV-nuzal is about node.quality / edge.provenance). Re-parented to INV-rukor, the row that owns derived_from.\n\nFiled from the per-site reading: WI-judov (ruby_ffi self-loop), WI-mofih (swift_objc dangling ids), WI-vojur (wasm_bindgen 0-0 file id), WI-gulud (react_component fabricated src)."  # 8832
